{number: 43}
{title: Rock of Ages, Cleft for Me}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Rock of Ages, cleft for me,
Let me [F] hide my-[C] self in [G7] Thee;
Let the [C] water and the blood,
From Thy [F] wounded [C] side which [G7] flowed,
Be of [C] sin the double cure,
Save from [F] wrath and [C] make [G7] me [C] pure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Could my tears forever flow,
Could my [F] zeal no [C] languor [G7] know,
These for [C] sin could not atone;
Thou must [F] save, and [C] Thou a-[G7] lone:
In my [C] hand no price I bring,
Simply [F] to Thy [C] cross [G7] I [C] cling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] While I draw this fleeting breath,
When my [F] eyes shall [C] close in [G7] death,
When I [C] rise to worlds unknown,
And be-[F] hold Thee [C] on Thy [G7] throne,
Rock of [C] Ages, cleft for me,
Let me [F] hide my-[C] self in [G7] Thee. [C]
{end_of_verse}
